  "limitations": [
    "This is a complete-output API comparator against statically linked libjpeg-turbo3.2.1. It does not replace ordinary CLI/djpeg streaming-output comparisons or establish the whole goal achieved.",
    "Both paths retain compressed input and an equally sized/typed complete output. Admitted DCT outputs may differ by one sample value; same-output memory means equal layout/precision/full retention, not universal byte identity against libjpeg. All five lossless cases are exact.",
    "Every timing process has one every-sample full-output preflight; measured iterations retain the qualified edge checks. Four RGB cases each have maximum difference3 versus tolerance2 and are excluded from timing/RSS.",
    "Timings remain provisional under observed host VM and other process activity. Noise8 gains0.77/3.42percent are near parity; single-worker2048DCT remains13.38/13.29percent slower.",
    "RSS values are medians of three fresh process high-water measurements, not logical allocation counts. Baseline/candidateRSS was a separate fresh paired run with no ca0 timing; its small ties/increases are retained and not pooled with current-vs-libjpeg samples.",
    "The ca0-to6e comparison spans several production changes and cannot attribute RSS reduction to the two-line empty-array constructor repair alone. Runtime stack, allocator and code-page contributions require measurement; source payload counts do not establish a causal RSS breakdown."
  ]
